WEBVTT

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.270
I'm a little scared myself.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:09.270
You know that nervous feeling you got before you got married, right?

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:14.210
"What if I don't get along with his family?"

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:15.030
I know.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.270
Right?

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:21.500
But his parents, and his brother and sister...

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.750
They all seem like such nice people.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:28.290
It's almost as if there's some kind of mistake,

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:32.800
like I'll have to pay back all this happiness sometime later.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:35.930
I never knew there was anything like this.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.310
I don't even think many of the villagers know about this.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.560
We'll be safe here, right?

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.020
They probably won't be able to find us anytime soon.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:48.110
Let's go.

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:07.700
O flower, parched in the light of dawn,

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:11.380
reaching for the unfallen rain,

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:18.430
fall into a wakeless sleep.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:32.340
Someone calls out softly for a paradise of darkness.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:33.990
Is it a lie or a dream?

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:35.970
Either way, it's already lost.

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:42.140
What do you gain by putting forth your heart?

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:46.210
Looking through those eyes,

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:49.310
life is foolish and fleeting enough to snatch away.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:52.840
Will today be the day you grieve the end

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:56.050
which comes to us all?

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:59.650
The calendula which sings of the abyss

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:03.310
silently blooms full.

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:06.480
Hatred and sadness

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.190
are bound together in those eyes.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:13.330
The calendula which sings of demise

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:16.940
is watered by solitude,

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:20.180
reaching for the unfallen rain,

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:49.440
There's no mistaking it.

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:51.630
So we're going in?

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:52.500
Yeah.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:54.440
Hasegawa-san.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.240
You gonna be okay?

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.200
Yeah, I'm just a little worn out.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:03.200
No one in your family's been afflicted... Must be frickin' rough.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:06.110
I don't have time to be worn out.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:10.430
We're getting revenge for your father.

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:12.330
You should come along.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:28.280
Wow, this would be a great hiding place for them.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:29.280
Yeah.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.350
We're not irrigating now, so there's no water.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:34.490
Probably seemed like a real good idea.

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:39.360
But they're fools for hiding here.

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:40.990
Hey, is anything there?

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.820
Looks like things are about to get interesting.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:01.880
Look at that!

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:04.920
There they are.

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:13.400
It's Yuzuki-san from the library.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:14.670
And next to him is...

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:16.900
Who's that?

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:21.400
Hey, isn't that the Shuuji-kun of the Gotoda family?

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:28.370
Yeah, the first one who died this summer...

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:33.530
We found those corpses in
Yamairi the day of his wake.

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:35.460
The one in the middle's...

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.540
We don't need to name them!

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:39.170
But...

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:42.920
These are demons. Terrible demons!

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:46.940
They're our enemies! They killed my father without a thought!

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:48.180
That's all we need to know!

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:51.620
We don't need to know who they are or where they're from!

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:54.240
We may have known them, sure,

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.190
but they're something else now!

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:59.720
These aren't the people we used to know!

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:05.250
Or would your friends be going around killing people?!

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.700
They're not human anymore!

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:13.350
Naming them is just gonna give us funny ideas!

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:14.200
You're right.

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:19.950
Can you give me a hand, Hasegawa-san?

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:21.090
O-Okay.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:40.390
I can't do it.

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:42.510
I owe Yuzuki-san so much.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:44.270
I just can't do it.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.110
That doesn't matter!

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:15.390
They're emotionless, so why show them mercy?!

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:19.860
Kill your emotions.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:22.150
Fight fire with fire!

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:23.870
Sorry.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:25.530
I'll do the next one.

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:49.180
I'll do the one after.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:57.560
Yuzuki!

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.190
Fucker scared me!

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:28.340
That fucker scared me!

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.340
Hell yeah, he did...

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:38.720
What's going on?

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.120
It sounds fun.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:43.600
It's not fun. There's something wrong!

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.150
They rise at night, right?

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:47.250
Yeah, I think.

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:50.010
We'll split up. Form the men into two squads.

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:51.680
One group kills inside.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:54.040
The other carries them out.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.890
Women, you help carry.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:56.620
Got it?

00:07:56.980 --> 00:07:58.710
We have weapons!

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.220
We don't have to be afraid of them rushing the exit!

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:02.130
Let's get cracking!

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:08.340
Are you going to be okay?

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:10.590
It's not like we have any choice...

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:13.000
Yeah.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.280
You can make it through this.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:15.370
Yeah...

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:36.870
They're coming!

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:38.410
They're getting closer!

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:40.160
They'll find us!

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.560
Look at all that blood!

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:53.320
They must have gotten most of the others.

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:54.340
We've got to run away!

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:55.050
Wait!

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:02.060
Don't tell anyone, but I never liked this guy.

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:05.940
All right, give me a hand.

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:11.070
I've hated you since I was a kid!

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:16.070
Don't you feel that way about anyone?

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:18.220
All right! Take 'em up!

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:25.510
Ebuchi-san!

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:27.310
Let's go.

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:29.600
We'll take out their lights.

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:32.510
With no light, they won't be able to see anything.

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:35.340
If we do that, we can slip away into the night.

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:40.920
Man, the ceilings down here are low.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:42.990
This is killing my back.

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:45.350
Let's get going!

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:50.610
Maybe we should trade with the lifters.

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:52.570
Yeah, let's.

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:55.740
If we don't, we'll be stuck down here until dawn.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.170
What?

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:09.000
Hey, you're that cop!

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:13.000
They're attacking!

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:15.630
Hold your ground!

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:17.250
We can take them!

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:00.550
Son of a...

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:05.130
Hold your ground!

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:07.680
Kill them! I don't care how, just kill them!

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:24.190
Dr. Ebuchi!

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:36.960
Were you bitten?

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:39.960
Let's get the hell outta here.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:43.220
S-Stop it!

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:48.140
Stop! It just nipped me!

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:49.980
I'm fine! I'll be okay!

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.030
How do we know that?!

00:11:52.030 --> 00:11:53.290
I'll be okay!

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:55.770
Didn't you hear the doctor?!

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:57.450
The doctor, huh.

00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:58.850
You hear that from him?

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:00.860
Nope, nothing like it.

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:03.270
Really! It's the truth!

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:04.770
I'll be fine!

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:07.870
They all died, didn't the—

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:11.090
That's bullshit!

00:12:11.090 --> 00:12:12.870
If you're going to lie, be a better liar!

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:21.510
Don't let him go! He's not human anymore!

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:25.020
I'm still fine!

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:27.490
If we let him go, he'll just make things worse!

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:29.010
Kill him!

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:30.810
Over here!

00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:38.030
Over here!

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:48.620
Dear...

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:52.480
Let's go home.

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:56.550
No. If we do...

00:12:58.620 --> 00:12:59.700
What's wrong?

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:02.360
Is that...

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:03.420
Yeah.

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:06.230
I thought it was absurd,

00:13:06.230 --> 00:13:10.250
just something out of the movies, so I...

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:13.410
I didn't believe in anything.

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:15.940
I thought everything was relative.

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:22.380
They're coming full force!

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:23.570
So what?!

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:26.030
What?!

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:29.000
What's wrong, Nao-san?

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:31.200
Nothing...

00:13:38.620 --> 00:13:39.830
What's your problem?

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:42.090
What are you doing?!

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:46.720
Nao-san!

00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:51.220
It's a dead end!

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:52.710
What?!

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:55.990
What do we do?

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:57.230
How should I know?!

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:59.210
If we can't fit through there...

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:07.240
Have they gone mad?

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:37.360
The ones from before...

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:38.910
If we don't chase them down, they'll get away.

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:40.010
Don't worry.

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:40.880
Huh?

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:45.010
It gets so narrow, not even a kid could crawl through.

00:14:46.520 --> 00:14:49.140
I'm being punished...

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:50.130
What?

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:51.910
I'm being punished!

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:56.710
Dad and Mom... My husband, even Susumu...

00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:59.460
I killed them all!

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:02.520
If you hadn't, you would've died!

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:06.790
I just wanted everyone to be happy...

00:15:11.030 --> 00:15:11.930
Hurry up!

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:18.100
I'm sorry! I'm so sorry!

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:20.890
I'm so sorry! I'm so sorry!

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.440
I'm so sorry!

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:24.020
Sasaki-san!

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:25.650
It's a dead end!

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:27.490
You're holding me back!

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:33.200
Please! Stop pushing!

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:35.070
Stop it!

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:36.200
Move it!

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:44.910
What do we do? We're out of stakes!

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:46.680
And there's still lots of them left!

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:48.320
The sun is about to rise!

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:49.790
Oh, I see!

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:52.930
When the sun comes up, that'll do it!

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:53.840
I get it.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.410
Do something, Sasaki-san!

00:16:00.410 --> 00:16:00.690
Please!

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:01.770
Move it! Move it!
Please!

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:02.130
Move it! Move it!

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:04.350
I can't! Stop pushing!

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:05.900
I'm next!

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:09.730
Move! Please, move!

00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:16.410
Let go of me!

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:23.500
It's my fault.

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.120
I let my husband die.

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:26.830
I killed Susumu.

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:29.380
I killed Mom and Dad.

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:32.280
I thought they'd rise.

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:34.880
I thought we'd be together forever.

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:38.300
I'm the only one who rose.

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:40.410
That's my punishment.

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:43.480
I... I killed them all...

00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:58.030
Sadafumi-san?!

00:16:59.420 --> 00:17:00.820
Stop!

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:04.290
Sadafumi-san, it's me, Nao!

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.080
It's me! Nao!

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.750
Please let me go!

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:11.300
Please!

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:14.300
Don't hurt me!

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:17.090
Please! Stop!

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:19.300
Save me, Sasaki-san!

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:20.580
Nao.

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:26.110
I didn't really want to bring them with me.

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:27.990
I wanted to change back.

00:17:32.370 --> 00:17:34.100
But...

00:17:34.100 --> 00:17:35.610
I...

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:40.260
I'll never...

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:45.850
I'll never, ever make it back...

00:17:50.640 --> 00:17:53.340
And her son is just so cute!

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:57.190
I never used to like kids, but now...

00:17:57.190 --> 00:18:00.580
Sorry, I keep getting carried away with all this.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:02.590
Hasegawa-san, do you have any children?

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:06.850
He died in an accident.

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:10.900
That's why we moved out here.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:12.460
Oh...

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:14.860
I'm sorry I brought it up.

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:17.260
Don't worry about it.

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:20.870
Sorry, I need to stop going on about myself.

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:26.980
She's so insensitive.

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:28.940
Don't say that about people.

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:30.460
But...

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:32.860
Let's not get so caught up in our own grief that we ignore that of others.

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:35.370
I didn't mean it that way.

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:37.600
Maybe not, but it sounded like it.

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:40.890
Sorry.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:44.380
I'm sure she has her own problems.

00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:47.130
We should try and be the kind of people who can help with them.

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:50.640
That might take some doing.

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:52.920
It's not that tough.

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:54.280
We'll be fine.

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:58.470
I feel like, living here, it'll just happen naturally.

00:18:58.470 --> 00:18:59.640
You're right.

00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:01.770
Everyone here is just so nice.

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:05.730
What, him too?

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:08.660
This just ain't right...

00:19:11.260 --> 00:19:13.190
All we have to do now is wait.

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:16.820
It's almost time.

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:52.550
Stop!

00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:53.230
Save me!

00:19:58.000 --> 00:19:58.960
No!

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:20.750
Dear...

00:20:28.780 --> 00:20:29.760
Hey, he's...

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:38.970
Hasegawa-san...

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:41.760
I told him we could stop, but...

00:21:07.230 --> 00:21:08.030
I'll be fine.

00:21:09.590 --> 00:21:11.760
It's not that hard.

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:40.890
Enveloped in darkness, I snuff my breath.

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:48.170
Clad in the darkness, I suddenly grin.

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:55.970
It's just my imagination; no one knows you.

00:21:56.010 --> 00:22:02.650
I'm just staring at the moon.

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:11.840
Ah, I haunt the endless night.

00:22:12.290 --> 00:22:18.440
Ah, I just dream a dream of you.

00:22:19.820 --> 00:22:26.650
Ah, I haunt the endless night.

00:22:27.290 --> 00:22:34.460
Ah, I just dream a dream of you.

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:55.680
If the mob comes rushing in,

00:22:56.140 --> 00:22:59.060
I must protect Sunako,

00:22:59.540 --> 00:23:01.640
even if I'm killed.

00:23:02.940 --> 00:23:06.820
Perhaps I'll be able to carry her away.

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:12.820
If Sunako falls into her sleep, it will likely be our parting.

00:23:14.320 --> 00:23:20.960
At the very least, may that night fall gently.

00:23:21.560 --> 00:23:22.500
Om.
